{"status": "ok", "message-type": "work-list", "message-version": "1.0.0", "message": {"facets": {}, "total-results": 3380033, "items": [{"institution": [{"name": "Carleton University", "place": ["Ottawa, Ontario"]}], "indexed": {"date-parts": [[2025, 7, 4]], "date-time": "2025-07-04T04:13:01Z", "timestamp": 1751602381729, "version": "3.41.0"}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Carleton University", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "DOI": "10.22215/etd/2000-04415", "type": "dissertation", "created": {"date-parts": [[2018, 10, 4]], "date-time": "2018-10-04T20:10:16Z", "timestamp": 1538683816000}, "approved": {"date-parts": [[2000]]}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["A Universal closed-form high-speed interconnect model for general purpose circuit simulators."], "prefix": "10.22215", "author": [{"given": "Xin", "family": "Li", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "9479", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2025, 7, 3]], "date-time": "2025-07-03T19:20:08Z", "timestamp": 1751570408000}, "score": 29.920626, "degree": ["Master of Engineering"], "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://hdl.handle.net/20.500.14718/33408"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[null]]}, "references-count": 0, "alternative-id": ["MQ48471"], "URL": "https://doi.org/10.22215/etd/2000-04415"}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 6, 12]], "date-time": "2026-06-12T16:03:53Z", "timestamp": 1781280233077, "version": "3.54.1"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2025, 4, 11]]}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE)", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2025, 4, 11]], "date-time": "2025-04-11T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1744329600000}, "content-version": "unspecified", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "abstract": "<jats:p>The increasing popularity of Large Language Models (LLMs) in the medical field has sparked discussions around the need for domain-specific training for medical tasks. This study aims to present a detailed comparison and evaluation of medical and general-purpose LLMs using three medical data sets (PubMedQA, BioASQ, and WikiDoc) comprising around 11,000 question-and-answer pairs. Across few-and zero-shot question-answer prompts and 8 models, 182,944 prompts were tested. We compared four domain-specific models (Meditron-7B, BioMistral-7B, MedAlpaca-13B, and PMC-LLaMA-13B) against four generalized instruction-tuned models (Ministral-8B-Instruct, Gemma 2-9B-it, Vicuna-13B v1.5, and Llama 3-8B-Instruct) using Semantic Similarity, BERTScore, and SimCSE. The study aims to shed light on whether it is necessary to develop domain-specific models-not just for medical tasks but for other industries as well.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.36227/techrxiv.174439863.35906289/v1", "type": "posted-content", "created": {"date-parts": [[2025, 4, 11]], "date-time": "2025-04-11T15:11:03Z", "timestamp": 1744384263000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Medical VS General-Purpose LLMS: Reassessing Domain Specialization in Healthcare"], "prefix": "10.36227", "author": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-4484-6751", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Daniel Quillan", "family": "Roxas", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "Applied Data Science, TED University Ankara"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Hakan", "family": "Emekci", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Applied Data Science, TED University"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "263", "link": [{"URL": "https://www.techrxiv.org/doi/pdf/10.36227/techrxiv.174439863.35906289/v1", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 6, 12]